    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "\"Fox Fires on New Year's Eve at the Changing Tree in Oji\" is a color woodblock print by Utagawa Hiroshige, created in 1857. This work diverges from Hiroshige's typical themes, drawing instead from Japanese folklore. It depicts the gathering of foxes at the Changing Tree near the Oji Inari Shrine on New Year’s Eve, where they ignite flames that farmers interpret as omens for the upcoming harvest. The print employs various shades of gray to illustrate the scene, contrasted by the vibrant orange of the flames, while stars peek through the tree's bare branches, a reminder of the tree's enduring presence in Tokyo.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "歌川広重の1857年作「王子の変わり木における大晦日の狐火」は、彼の典型的なテーマから逸脱し、日本の民話に基づいています。作品は、大晦日に王子稲荷神社近くの変わり木に集まる狐たちを描き、彼らが点火する炎を農民が来年の収穫の予兆として解釈します。さまざまな灰色の色調がシーンを表現し、炎の鮮やかなオレンジが対比を生み出します。星々が木の裸の枝を通してわずかに見え、今も東京に残るこの木の存在を思い起こさせます。"
    },
