    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "Plum Garden at Kameido, created by Utagawa Hiroshige in 1857, is a striking color woodblock print from the series \"One Hundred Famous Views of Edo.\" This work is celebrated for its innovative composition and vibrant colors, particularly the reddish sky that adds a dramatic flair. The prominent tree depicted is renowned in Edo (modern-day Tokyo) for its unique shape, likened to a sleeping dragon. Hiroshige's design has left a lasting impact, inspiring artists such as Vincent van Gogh, who famously adapted this scene in his 1887 painting, Flowering Plum Orchard (After Hiroshige).",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "1857年に歌川広重が制作した「亀戸梅屋敷」は、「江戸名所百景」シリーズの中で特に認知度の高い色木版画です。革新的な構図と鮮やかな色彩、特に赤い空が印象的です。この作品に描かれた木は、江戸（現在の東京）で最も有名な木とされ、眠るドラゴンに似ていると言われています。広重のデザインは後にフィンセント・ファン・ゴッホに影響を与え、1887年に「広重の後に描かれた花咲く梅の果樹園」として再解釈されました。"
    },
