    "width": 814,
    "height": 1200,
    "museum": "Art Institute of Chicago",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/34096",
    "license": "CC0 1.0 (public-domain image)",
    "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
    "licenseBasis": "Art Institute of Chicago: official API field is_public_domain=true; image field image_id is present; verified 2026-11-23",
    "sourceImageUrl": "https://www.artic.edu/iiif/2/15e90d2e-ba4f-4fff-f784-fc84f4bbfe0a/full/843,/0/default.jpg",
    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "In Utagawa Hiroshige's 1856 color woodblock print \"Kinryuzan Temple at Asakusa,\" a striking red gate and lantern emerge against a backdrop of pristine white snow, guiding the way to Kinryūzan Temple. This vivid color contrast symbolizes renewal, resonating with the auspiciousness of the New Year in Japan. Although the scene is devoid of the usual crowds and vendors that would typically fill the path to the temple, the presence of the lantern evokes the lively atmosphere of Sensōji Temple in Asakusa, a bustling entertainment district. Hiroshige captures a moment of serene beauty, inviting contemplation amidst the winter stillness.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "歌川広重の1856年の色木版画「浅草金龍山」では、白い雪の背景に映える赤い門と提灯が金龍山寺への道を示しています。この鮮やかな色の対比は、日本の新年の吉兆を象徴しています。通常は賑わう店や屋台が並ぶ道が人影もなく静まり返っている様子は、天候や時間帯によるものかもしれませんが、提灯の存在は浅草の賑やかな浅草寺の雰囲気を呼び起こします。広重は冬の静けさの中で、穏やかな美しさの瞬間を捉えています。"
    },
