    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "This woodblock print by Okumura Masanobu, created around 1710 during the Edo period, depicts Murasaki Shikibu, the esteemed author of \"The Tale of Genji,\" Japan's most celebrated novel. Often portrayed in moments of reflection, she is shown here gazing out over Lake Biwa, a serene backdrop that complements her literary pursuits. The scene captures her at a low table, surrounded by blank sheets of paper, brushes, and ink, symbolizing her creative process and the tranquility that inspired her writing after her retreat from court life.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "この木版画は、江戸時代の1710年頃に奥村政信によって制作されたもので、著名な小説『源氏物語』の作者、紫式部を描いています。彼女は湖の景色を眺めながら、創作活動の合間に静かなひとときを過ごしています。低いテーブルの上には白紙、筆、墨が置かれ、彼女の創作過程と、隠遁生活から得た静けさを象徴しています。"
    },
