    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "This hand-colored woodblock print by Ishikawa Toyonobu, created around 1748, depicts the actor Sanogawa Ichimatsu I in his role as Hisamatsu from the play \"The Eternal Soga of the Green Gate,\" performed at the Nakamura theater in February 1743. Ichimatsu's outer coat, or haori, features a distinctive brown-and-black checked pattern that he popularized, making it a recurring motif in his portraits. The striking contrast between the haori and the white kimono adorned with pink plum blossoms and seals enhances the visual impact of the piece, showcasing the elegance of Edo-period theater attire.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "この手彩色の浮世絵は、1748年頃に石川豊信によって制作され、役者の佐野川市松一が「緑の門の永遠の曽我」での久松を演じる姿を描いています。この芝居は1743年2月に中村座で上演されました。市松の外套（羽織）は、彼が流行させた茶黒のチェック模様で、彼の肖像画にも多く見られます。羽織と白い着物の間にある梅の花と印章の模様との対比が、作品の視覚的なインパクトを高めています。"
    },
