    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "Katsushika Hokusai's color woodblock print, \"Tenji Tenno (The Emperor Tenji),\" created around 1835/36, depicts the first poet in the series \"One Hundred Poems by One Hundred Poets Explained by the Nurse.\" The artwork illustrates a poignant moment in the life of Emperor Tenji, who reigned from 668 to 671 and was instrumental in establishing Japan's first civil law code. The scene captures the emperor taking shelter from a sudden rainstorm in a makeshift hut, reflecting on the hardships faced by his subjects. His poem, expressing empathy for those toiling in the fields, resonates with the viewer, highlighting the connection between leadership and the welfare of the people.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "葛飾北斎の色彩木版画「天智天皇」は、1835/36年頃に制作され、「百人一首の歌を看護婦が解説する」シリーズの最初の詩人を描いています。この作品は、668年から671年まで在位した天智天皇が、突然の雨から稲田の仮小屋に避難する場面を表現しています。彼の詩は、日々の苦労を強いられる民への思いやりを伝え、リーダーシップと民の福祉とのつながりを浮き彫りにしています。"
    },
