    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "Abe no Nakamaro, depicted in this color woodblock print by Katsushika Hokusai, is the seventh poet in the series One Hundred Poems by One Hundred Poets. Created around 1833, the artwork shows a mature Nakamaro seated on the terrace of a Chinese palace, surrounded by friends. Having spent over thirty years in China, he never returned to his home near Nara. The poem referenced in this print, directed toward the moon, reflects his enduring feelings of exile despite his successful career abroad.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "葛飾北斎によるこの色彩木版画『阿倍仲麻呂』は、『百人一首』の第七詩人を描いています。1833年頃に制作されたこの作品では、仲麻呂が中国の宮殿のテラスに座り、友人たちと共にいます。彼は30年以上中国に滞在し、奈良の故郷には戻りませんでした。この版画に示された詩は、月に向けられたもので、成功したキャリアにもかかわらず、彼の exile に対する思いが反映されています。"
    },
