    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "This color woodblock print by Katsushika Hokusai depicts Sojo Henjo, the twelfth poet in the series \"One Hundred Poems by One Hundred Poets Explained by the Nurse.\" Created around 1835/36, the artwork illustrates a scene from Henjo's early life as a member of the imperial family and a court minister, prior to his ascension as a priest. Set in springtime at court, it features a noblewoman performing a dance, traditionally associated with the autumn harvest, celebrating the rice crop planted by the emperor. Henjo is later recognized as one of the six Poetic Immortals for his modern poetry.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "葛飾北斎によるこの色彩木版画は、「看護師による百人一首」の第十二詩人、僧正遍昭を描いています。1835年頃に制作されたこの作品は、遍昭が皇族であり宮廷大臣であった頃の春の宮廷の様子を表現しています。貴族の女性が、天皇が春に植えた稲作の成功を祝う秋の収穫に関連する舞を披露しています。遍昭は後に、現代詩で知られる六歌仙の一人となります。"
    },
