    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "This color woodblock print, titled \"Ariwara no Narihira,\" is part of Katsushika Hokusai's series \"A True Mirror of Chinese and Japanese Poems,\" created around 1830. The artwork is inspired by the ninety-fourth poem from the renowned anthology \"One Hundred Poems by One Hundred Poets,\" attributed to Privy Councilor Masatsune. The poem evokes a scene of autumnal chill and the sounds of a distant hamlet at night, though it is curiously linked to the more famous figure of Narihira. Hokusai's print captures the essence of this poetic imagery, blending visual art with literary tradition.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "この色彩木版画「在原業平」は、葛飾北斎の「中国と日本の詩の真実の鏡」シリーズの一部で、1830年頃に制作されました。この作品は、著名な「百人一首」の第94首に触発されており、詩は内大臣正経に帰属しています。詩は秋の寒さと夜の遠い集落の音を描写していますが、なぜかより有名な業平に結びつけられています。北斎の版画は、この詩的なイメージの本質を捉え、視覚芸術と文学の伝統を融合させています。"
    },
