    "sourceImageUrl": "https://www.artic.edu/iiif/2/2909d94b-9066-a9cd-65fc-665bb622c1b7/full/843,/0/default.jpg",
    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "The Poetess Ono no Komachi, created by Katsushika Hokusai around 1810, is part of the series \"Six Immortal Poets,\" which celebrates renowned figures from Japan’s classical literary tradition. Ono no Komachi, the only female poet among these six, is depicted in elegant ninth-century court attire, gazing over her shoulder from behind a standing screen. Her poem reflects on the fickleness of love, likening it to the changing hues of a flower. This print captures both her beauty and the complexity of her character, illustrating the dualities that define her legacy.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "葛飾北斎による「六歌仙」シリーズの一部である「女流詩人小野小町」は、約1810年に制作されました。小町は六人の中で唯一の女性詩人で、華やかな九世紀の宮廷衣装を身にまとい、屏風の後ろから振り返る姿が描かれています。彼女の詩は愛の移ろいやすさを花の色の変化に例えています。この版画は、彼女の美しさと複雑な人間性を捉え、彼女の遺産を形作る二面性を表現しています。"
    },
