    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "In this color woodblock print by Katsushika Hokusai, titled \"Harumichi no Tsuraki,\" the thirty-second poet in the series \"One Hundred Poems by One Hundred Poets Explained by the Nurse,\" we see a serene scene inspired by Tsuraki's poem composed in 920 while crossing Mount Shiga. The artwork captures a lovely day transitioning to evening, with woodcutters at work and a fisherman casting his net among the maple leaves caught in the mountain stream. A mother guides her son, who carries a pet turtle, across a plank bridge, embodying the harmony of nature and daily life.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "葛飾北斎によるこの色彩木版画「春道の連木」は、「看護婦による百人一首」の第32詩人を描いています。920年に滋賀山を越えた際に詠まれた連木の詩に触発された作品で、夕暮れに向かう穏やかな日を描写しています。木こりが作業を続け、漁師が山の流れの中で楓の葉を捕まえながら網を投げます。母親が息子を導き、彼は亀を運びながら板橋を渡る姿が、自然と日常生活の調和を表現しています。"
    },
