    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "Catching Fireflies, created by Suzuki Harunobu around 1767, is a color woodblock print that exemplifies the early years of full-color printing in Japan. The artwork features two figures engaged in the delicate act of catching fireflies, set against a flat black night sky. Notably, the fireflies lack any glow, directing the viewer's attention to the intricate and vibrant patterns of the clothing worn by the young man and woman. This piece highlights Harunobu's skill in combining elegant design with the cultural practices of his time.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "鈴木春信の「蛍捕り」は、約1767年に制作された色彩木版画で、日本の初期のフルカラー印刷を代表する作品です。夜空は平坦な黒で描かれ、蛍は光を放たず、若い男女の着物の複雑で華やかなデザインに視線が集まります。この作品は、春信の優れたデザイン技術と当時の文化的習慣を融合させたものです。"
    },
