    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "In \"Ono no Komachi by the Waterfall,\" part of the series \"The Seven Fashionable Aspects of Komachi,\" artist Suzuki Harunobu captures a moment of beauty and reflection. The print depicts two elegantly dressed women admiring cherry blossoms at Kiyomizu Temple in Kyoto during their peak bloom. This scene draws on the legend of Ono no Komachi, a figure known for her visits to the temple, possibly to meet a lover. The print features Kiyomizu Temple and its iconic three waterfalls, symbolizing the passage of time, alongside a poignant poem reflecting on aging and the enduring nature of the waterfall.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "鈴木春信の「滝の近くの小町」は、「風流八つ子七小町」シリーズの一部です。桜が満開の清水寺で、二人の華やかな女性が桜を楽しむ様子が描かれています。この場面は、恋人に会うために寺を訪れた小野小町の伝説に基づいています。作品には清水寺とその三つの滝が描かれ、時の流れを象徴しています。詩は、老いと滝の変わらぬ姿を対比させています。"
    },
