    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "The Hole in the Wall, created by Suzuki Harunobu in 1765, is a captivating color woodblock print that serves as a calendar for that year, the second of the Meiwa era. The artwork intricately incorporates the numbers of the short months into the pattern of a girl’s robe, while the long months are represented in the man’s robe. This design draws inspiration from the Hole-in-the-Wall affair, a narrative from the Tales of Ise, which recounts the secret visit of the poet Narihira to the empress through a crumbling palace wall, leading to his eventual exile.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "鈴木春信の「壁の穴」は1765年に制作された色刷り木版画で、同年のカレンダーとして機能しています。短い月の数字は少女の着物の模様に、長い月の数字は男性の着物に描かれています。このデザインは、平安時代の詩人・在原業平が皇后に密かに訪れた際の「壁の穴」の逸話に触発されています。業平は崩れた宮殿の壁を通って入った後、発覚し、北日本に追放されました。"
    },
