    "licenseBasis": "Art Institute of Chicago: official API field is_public_domain=true; image field image_id is present; verified 2026-11-23",
    "sourceImageUrl": "https://www.artic.edu/iiif/2/1824a39b-9c8c-b246-d14e-5d796874cabc/full/843,/0/default.jpg",
    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "Suzuki Harunobu's color woodblock print, \"Sugawara Michizane Going into Exile,\" created around 1763/64, depicts the exiled scholar Sugawara Michizane seated on an ox. Discredited by the Fujiwara clan and ordered to Kyushu, Michizane gazes over the sea and a waning moon, reflecting on his separation from the capital. The accompanying cartouche highlights his poignant thoughts, emphasizing his longing for the moon that illuminates his former home. Michizane, who passed away in Dazaifu in 903, is celebrated annually at a Shinto festival held at his tomb in the eighth month, honoring his legacy as a distinguished poet and scholar.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "鈴木春信の色刷り木版画「菅原道真の追放」は、約1763/64年に制作されました。追放された学者・菅原道真が牛に乗っている姿が描かれています。藤原氏によって失脚させられ、九州に命じられた道真は、海と月を見つめ、都を思い馳せています。右側の長いカルトゥーシュには、彼の切ない思いが記されています。道真は903年に太宰府で亡くなり、毎年8月に彼の墓で行われる神道の祭りで、その業績が称えられています。"
    },
