    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "This folded surimono print, created by Nakajima Raishô in the 1850s, exemplifies the unique characteristics of Japanese color woodblock prints. Often discarded and rarely preserved, such prints were not highly regarded in Japan or among Western collectors during the 19th century. Raishô, who designed this piece, also contributed a personal poem alongside the image of a kite, which symbolizes the New Year. Kite flying was a popular tradition at that time. The print's intricate design unfolds gradually, revealing its beauty as it is opened, showcasing the artistry of folding techniques used for transport and presentation.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "中島雷翔によるこの折りたたみ式の摺物は1850年代に制作され、日本の色彩木版画の特性を示しています。こうした作品はしばしば廃棄され、保存されることは稀で、19世紀の日本や西洋のコレクターの間でも高く評価されていませんでした。雷翔はこの作品に自身の詩を添え、凧のイメージを描いています。凧は新年の象徴であり、当時は凧揚げが盛んでした。印刷技術を駆使したこの作品は、開くにつれてその美しさが徐々に現れます。"
    },
