    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "A Collection of Flowers and Birds (Kacho zukushi) is a woodblock-printed book by Hishikawa Moronobu, created in 1683 during the Edo period. This exquisite volume features ten sheets that showcase twenty-six meticulously rendered birds and flowers. Notably, one of the illustrations captures a group of cranes at the seashore, exemplifying Moronobu's extraordinary attention to detail and his ability to blend natural beauty with artistic precision. This work is a significant representation of Japanese culture and artistry from the period.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "「花鳥尽し」は、江戸時代の1683年に著作された、菱川師宣による木版印刷の本です。この美しい巻物は、26種の鳥と花を描いた10枚のシートで構成されています。特に、海岸にいる鶴の群れが描かれ、師宣の細部への驚くべきこだわりと自然美の表現が際立っています。この作品は、当時の日本文化と芸術を代表する重要な作品です。"
    },
