    "description": "This artwork features Ichikawa Ebizô V as Togashi Saemon and Ichikawa Danjûrô VIII as Musashibô Benkei, captured in a moment from the kabuki play Kanjinchô (The Subscription List). Created by Utagawa Kunisada I, also known as Toyokuni III, around 1852, this piece is part of the series Eighteen Great Kabuki Plays (Jûhachiban no uchi). Rendered in ink on paper, it exemplifies the rich tradition of kabuki theater in Japan, showcasing the dramatic expressions and costumes that characterize this art form.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "この作品は、歌舞伎の演目『勧進帳』の一場面を描いており、右に市川海老蔵五代目の富樫左衛門、左に市川団十郎八代目の武蔵坊弁慶が描かれています。歌川国貞（豊国三代目）によって1852年頃に制作され、シリーズ『十八番の内』の一部です。紙にインクで描かれたこの作品は、日本の歌舞伎の伝統を体現し、劇的な表情や衣装が特徴です。"
    },
