    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "In 1873, Claude Monet painted \"The Artist's House at Argenteuil,\" capturing a serene moment in his family life. Set in their vine-covered home, the artwork features his young son, Jean, playing with a hoop, while his wife, Camille, stands in the doorway. The lush garden and pleasant weather reflect a sense of tranquility, foreshadowing the renowned garden Monet would later cultivate at Giverny. This period marked a time of financial stability for the artist, bolstered by successful sales through the Parisian art dealer Paul Durand-Ruel.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "1873年、クロード・モネは「アルジャンテイユの画家の家」を描き、家族の穏やかな瞬間を捉えました。つる植物に覆われた家の前で、息子のジャンがフープで遊び、妻のカミーユがドアのところに立っています。手入れの行き届いた庭と穏やかな天候は、静けさを感じさせ、モネが後にジヴェルニーで育てることになる名高い庭を予感させます。この時期、モネはパリの画商ポール・デュラン＝リュエルとの成功した取引により、経済的安定を享受していました。"
    },
