    "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "In \"Jean Renoir Sewing,\" painted between 1899 and 1900, Pierre-Auguste Renoir captures a tender moment with his son, Jean, who served as his model from a young age. The painting reflects the Impressionist style, characterized by its vibrant colors and soft brushwork. Jean, with his long, golden hair, was encouraged to keep it that way until he turned seven, much to his chagrin. During the modeling session, the children’s nanny, Gabrielle, suggested he occupy himself by sewing a satin coat for his toy camel, adding a charming narrative to this intimate portrait.",
    "descriptionTranslations": {
      "ja": "ピエール＝オーギュスト・ルノワールの「ジャン・ルノワールの縫い物」は1899年から1900年にかけて描かれ、息子ジャンとの親密な瞬間を捉えています。印象派のスタイルで、鮮やかな色彩と柔らかな筆致が特徴です。長い金髪を持つジャンは、7歳になるまでその髪型を保つように言われ、恥ずかしがっていました。モデルの間、子供の乳母ガブリエルが、彼が玩具のキャメルのためにサテンのコートを縫うことで時間をつぶすよう提案しました。"
    },
